\title{metascience: catalogue and shared infrastructure for open metascience tools}
\description{
The package is the hub of a set of independent tools that study research.
It does not re-implement them: it tells you what exists (\code{\link[=ms_catalogue]{ms_catalogue()}}),
what is installed (\code{\link[=ms_status]{ms_status()}}), and gives every tool the same small
foundation:
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item persistent identifiers: \code{\link[=ms_doi]{ms_doi()}}, \code{\link[=ms_orcid]{ms_orcid()}}, \code{\link[=ms_ror]{ms_ror()}},
\code{\link[=ms_identify]{ms_identify()}};
\item one vocabulary for result statuses and evidence levels:
\code{\link[=ms_vocabulary]{ms_vocabulary()}}, \code{\link[=ms_harmonise_status]{ms_harmonise_status()}};
\item provenance: \code{\link[=ms_manifest]{ms_manifest()}} and \code{\link[=ms_write_manifest]{ms_write_manifest()}}.
}

Two rules run through the whole ecosystem. A result that cannot be verified
from the sources consulted is reported as unverifiable, never as zero or
"no". And a statistical signal is never presented as proof: anomalies,
inferred AI use and similar findings carry their evidence level.
}
